</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Emotional reactions to environmental risks: consequentialism versus ethical evaluation</article-title><source>Journal of Environmental Psychology</source><year>2003</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>212</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0272-4944(02)00114-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alderson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Farsides</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Examining ethics in practice: health service professionals' evaluations of in-hospital ethics seminars</article-title><source>Journal of Nursing Ethics</source><year>2002</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>518</fpage><lpage>531</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12238747</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ives</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Encounters with Experience: Empirical bioethics and the future</article-title><source>Health Care Analysis</source><year>2008</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18080836</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10728-007-0077-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ives</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Draper</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pattison</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Becoming a father/refusing fatherhood: An empirical bioethics approach to paternal responsibilities and rights</article-title><sour